# Evolution X Manifest Repository

This repository contains the manifest files for building Evolution X custom ROM.

## 📱 Device-Specific Builds

### Redmi Note 10s (rosemary/secret)

This repository includes a pre-configured setup for building Evolution X with LineageOS 23.0 kernel for the Redmi Note 10s.

**✅ Uses Official LineageOS Repositories** - No custom device trees needed!

**Files included:**
- `rosemary.xml` - Device manifest using official LineageOS sources
- `.github/workflows/build-rom.yml` - GitHub Actions workflow for automated builds
- `.github/workflows/sync-test.yml` - Manifest validation workflow
- `SIMPLIFIED_START.md` - ⭐ **START HERE** - Easy setup guide
- `BUILD_GUIDE.md` - Comprehensive building instructions
- `CUSTOMIZATION.md` - Customization options

**Quick Start:**
1. ⭐ **Read `SIMPLIFIED_START.md`** - Everything is ready!
2. Fork this repository
3. Run GitHub Actions workflow OR build locally
4. That's it! No device tree setup needed!

**Official Sources:**
- Device Tree: https://github.com/LineageOS/android_device_xiaomi_rosemary
- Kernel: https://github.com/LineageOS/android_kernel_xiaomi_mt6785 (lineage-23.0)

---

## 🔧 General Build Instructions

# Initialize local repository
```
repo init -u https://github.com/Evolution-X/manifest -b bka --git-lfs
```

# Add device manifest (for rosemary)
```
mkdir -p .repo/local_manifests
cp rosemary.xml .repo/local_manifests/
```

# Sync up
```
repo sync -c -j$(nproc --all) --force-sync --no-clone-bundle --no-tags
```

# Build

- Set up the build environment
```bash
. build/envsetup.sh
```

- Lunch a target
```bash
lunch lineage_rosemary-bp2a-userdebug
```

- To start compiling
```bash
m evolution
```

